# Build context for the mdqm images: the server image (./Dockerfile, task M08) and the mock API image
# (docker/api.Dockerfile, task D01). Keep it small: the server build copies pyproject.toml,
# README.md, src/ and wheelhouse/, so nothing else needs to travel to the daemon — which matters
# twice over here, because on a cluster the whole context is uploaded to an in-cluster builder.
# `wheelhouse/` is deliberately NOT ignored: the wheelhouse install mode reads it (air-gapped build).

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# local environments and per-session worktrees
.venv
venv
.worktrees

# build output
dist
build
*.egg-info

# tool caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.hypothesis

# local runtime state: never bake a developer's database, cache or spill files into an image
data
cache
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.log

# secrets and dev tokens
.env
.env.*
tokens.json
*.pem

# agent transcripts, plans and deployment manifests: irrelevant to the build and not ours to ship
.pi
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# not needed at build time (the images ship the package, the CLI, and nothing else)
tests
progress
plugin
docs
deploy
examples
TASKS.md
tasks.json
AGENT_PROMPT.md
SUMMARY_HE.md
